Phylogenetic Analysis of the Hemoglobin Beta (HBB) Gene

Explore the sequence conservation and evolutionary history of the HBB gene by analyzing homologs from different mammalian species using multiple sequence alignment and phylogenetic analysis.

Project Workflow

NCBI Database → BLASTx Search → MEGA 12 (ClustalW MSA) → MEGA 12 (Neighbor-Joining Tree) → iTOL Visualization

Step 1: Retrieve the HBB Sequence
Visit the NCBI database.
Search for Homo sapiens HBB.
Open the HBB gene/protein record.
Download the sequence in FASTA format.
Save the file as HBB_Human.fasta.

Deliverable:

FASTA sequence
Screenshot of the NCBI record
Step 2: Identify Homologous Sequences Using BLASTx
Open the BLASTx tool.
Paste the HBB FASTA sequence.
Run the search using default parameters.
Select 20-30 mammalian homologs with:
High Query Coverage
High Percentage Identity
Low E-value
Download the selected sequences in FASTA format.

Suggested Species

Human (Homo sapiens)
Chimpanzee (Pan troglodytes)
Gorilla (Gorilla gorilla)
Mouse (Mus musculus)
Rat (Rattus norvegicus)
Dog (Canis lupus familiaris)
Cow (Bos taurus)
Horse (Equus caballus)
Pig (Sus scrofa)
Rabbit (Oryctolagus cuniculus)

